Cash Management - 5 Days Hold Checking - Production Team
Within our current operations, whenever an account receives a credit—via ACH or cheque—the credited amount must be held back for five business days. Any debit or disbursement request may only be processed after this mandatory holding period has elapsed. Presently, this verification is performed manually by the production team each time a disbursement is requested, leading to delays, potential errors, and increased operational overhead.
Business Problem Statement:
We require an automated solution that can monitor account activity and accurately verify whether any credits have occurred within the last five business days. The tool should seamlessly check the account for recent credits and enforce the five-day hold for debits, thus streamlining our workflow, reducing manual intervention, and minimizing risk. This automation will enhance efficiency, ensure compliance with cash management policies, and provide real-time assurance of account status for both operational and regulatory needs.
This problem statement aligns with our ongoing efforts to modernize financial operations by leveraging real-time event-driven accounting practices, and supports the production team's need for secure, accurate, and scalable cash management processes.
Expected Output
•	Automated verification of account credits received within the last five business days.
•	Prevention of debit/disbursement processing until the five-day hold period is completed.
•	Real-time dashboard for production team to monitor account status, hold periods, and transaction eligibility.
•	Audit trail for compliance, with logs of credit, hold, and disbursement events.
•	Reduction in manual intervention, error rates, and operational delays.
•	Seamless integration with existing accounting and banking systems.

 
